{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Or a son it shall gore, or a daughter.</b> It mentions in this section a son or a daughter, a man or a woman — what it did not specify for you in other sections — to teach you that if the owner of the ox says, 'This woman was immodest,' 'the son and the daughter — their father did not guard them as required,' his words are nothing, and therefore the verse specified them. Another interpretation: for a free person there is no difference between an adult and a minor, but for a slave or a maidservant he is liable only for adults."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:35.454395836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}